Required minimal packages:
•	Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity.EntityFrameworkCore
o	Includes functionality for user registration and login, password recovery, roles, email confirmation and potential integration for external providers like google, facebooks, and twitter – something to think about.
•	Npasql.EntityFrameworkCore.PostgresSQL
o	Used to connect to the postgreASL database.
•	Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authenticatio.JwtBearer
o	JSON web token authentication (think similar to cookies)

Very helpful video tutorial: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=brxStRVyJiM
-- Because we are using PostgreSQL, you will want to ignore where he configures with MySQL. Your connection string should look something like this:
"ConnectionStrings": {
    "SecurityDb": "User ID=postgres;Password=password_;Host=localhost;Port=5433;Database=AspNetCoreIdentity;Pooling=true;"}
timestamp 5:39 Password requirements – 
	Required length: 15
	All other listed requirements should be set to true.
timestamp 8:05 Random key – 
You can generate a random key using this script in powershell:
[Convert]::ToBase64String((1..64 | ForEach-Object {Get-Random -Maximum 256}))
	Store the key as a secret and then reference – DO NOT paste directly into code.
